{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1475026874,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUxNzk2NjA1NTg=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/937","origin":"github"},"title":"'datalad install subds' installs into a detached HEAD","message":"as super/sub-datasets progress-forward, current version of a subds might be ahead of what installed locally super-dataset knows about.  Then when 'datalad install subds' is performed, it  installs that subdataset rightfully at the known position, but because its master (remote one) is ahead, it installs into a detached HEAD:\n\n``` shell\nhopa:~/datalad/openfmri/ds000030\n$\u003e git br\n* (HEAD detached at 3d9fc7e)\n  git-annex\n  master\n\n$\u003e git lg master\n*   890f095 - (origin/master, origin/HEAD, master) Merge branch 'incoming-processed' (24 hours ago) [Yaroslav Halchenko]\n|\\  \n| *   15f8bcf - [DATALAD] Added files from extracted archives (24 hours ago) [Yaroslav Halchenko]\n| |\\  \n| | * 19feafd - [DATALAD] removed: 25 (26 hours ago) [Yaroslav Halchenko]\n| * |   cff7f40 - [DATALAD] Added files from extracted archives (26 hours ago) [Yaroslav Halchenko]\n| |\\ \\  \n| | |/  \n```\n\nwhich of cause could be treated as a feature or a curse in terms of usability. I wonder if  we should\n- add `--updated` to install so it wouldn't install version as known to super, but rather just proceeds to current state/master and possibly marking itself as 'changed' in the eyes of the super.\n- should install always 'reset' master (or some other known remote branch name which known position is a predecessor of) to the position?\n\nthose all should be considered also in light that may be this RF should be joined with RF to support versioning specification for install calal","files":null}]}